    "prompt": "Solve $|2x-5|+3=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No solution.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}|2x-5|+3&=1\\\\|2x-5|&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nAn absolute value is a distance from zero, so it can never be negative. Neither case $2x-5=-2$ nor $-(2x-5)=-2$ can give a valid value of $x$, so there is no solution.",
